From d0a1bd0354e7d3b22a4fb0306f4c31825ecb6b8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Viand <alexander.viand@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:20:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [mlir][emitc] Lower the remaining <math.h> functions in
 MathToEmitC

MathToEmitC lowered only a dozen math ops to <math.h>/<cmath> calls, so
code using e.g. math.log, math.tanh or math.isnan could not reach EmitC
even though C and C++ provide these functions directly.

Add call patterns for tan, atan, sinh, cosh, tanh, asinh, acosh, atanh,
exp2, expm1, log, log2, log10, log1p, cbrt, erf, erfc, trunc, copysign
and fma, which follow the existing f32 `f` suffix (C) and `std::` (C++)
naming. Lower the classification ops isnan, isinf, isfinite and isnormal
to the macros of the same name, which take any floating-point type and
so carry no suffix in C. Lower math.sincos to separate sin and cos calls.

convert-math-to-emitc now also marks sqrt and roundeven illegal, which
it already had patterns for.
